[center][color=#ffff00][size=6][b]Hardest to Be on Growl FM[/b][/size][/color]
[i]Puts P.T. Adamczyk and Sora Lion's song on 89.7 Growl FM, where it should have been.[/i][/center]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Description[/b][/size][/color]
[b]Hardest to Be[/b] is one of the best pieces of music in Phantom Liberty, and you hear it once. It plays during a single quest, and then it is gone. Every other song on Growl FM you can put on in a car whenever you feel like it. Not that one.

That annoyed me enough to go looking, and it turns out the full recording, vocals and all, is sitting in your game files already. It is used by the apartment hangouts and by nothing else. Six of the seven tracks in that hangout playlist are ordinary radio songs from other stations. This one is the only one that never made it onto a dial.

So this mod puts it on Growl FM. It comes up in rotation like any other track on the station, at the same volume as the rest, with the artist and title on the HUD.

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]It ships no audio[/b][/size][/color]
The song is already installed on your machine. This mod is a few hundred bytes of soundbank and a script that tells the station the track exists. It does not contain, copy or redistribute any music, and it does not overwrite a single vanilla file.

[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Features[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][b]Plays in normal rotation.[/b] Nothing to activate and nothing to configure. Get in a car, tune to 89.7, and wait for it like any other song.
[*][b]The full song.[/b] Not the short section from the quest scene, and not the instrumental.
[*][b]Correct levels.[/b] The track hangs off Growl FM's own playlist, so it is mixed exactly like the station's other thirteen.
[*][b]Named properly.[/b] Shows as [font=Courier New]P.T. Adamczyk, Sora Lion - Hardest to Be[/font], with the artist credits taken from the game's own credits roll.
[*][b]All languages.[/b] The title is registered for every language the game ships.
[*][b]Safe to remove.[/b] Nothing is written to your save and no vanilla file is touched. Delete the folders and the station goes back to thirteen tracks.
[/list]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/23851]AudioXL[/url] - loads the soundbank.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4198]ArchiveXL[/url] - registers the track title.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]Redscript[/url]
[/list]
[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Optional[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/31920]RedLogger[/url] - the mod writes what it registered to [font=Courier New]r6\logs\mods\[/font]. Only needed if something is not working and you want to know why.
[/list]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
Install with your mod manager, or extract the archive into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder so you end up with:
[code]Cyberpunk 2077\archive\pc\mod\HardestToBeGrowlFM.archive
Cyberpunk 2077\archive\pc\mod\HardestToBeGrowlFM.archive.xl
Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\HardestToBeGrowlFM\HardestToBeGrowlFM.reds
Cyberpunk 2077\red4ext\plugins\AudioXL\sounds\HardestToBeGrowlFM\[/code]

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size][/color]
Delete those four paths. No save cleanup is needed.

[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]The station's track list is edited in memory as the game loads it, so no vanilla file is replaced and nothing conflicts with other mods that touch radio.
[*]Works alongside mods that add new stations, such as RadioXL and RadioExt. Those build their own stations; this one adds to a stock one.
[*]The track is added once. Loading a save made before installing is fine.
[/list]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][b]Hardest to Be[/b] written by P.T. Adamczyk, lyrics and vocals by Sora Lion. Music belongs to CD PROJEKT RED, and this mod plays your own copy of it.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/23851]AudioXL[/url] by DigitalVixen, which loads the soundbank.
[/list]
